# --- Scraped pages -----------------------------------------------------------
# Raw menu HTML stays OFF the repository, deliberately.
#
# Two reasons. A restaurant's page is their content, and republishing whole
# copies of it goes well beyond what this project needs. And the pages are
# large, change constantly, and would bloat the history for no benefit, since
# what the project is actually about is item names and prices.
#
# The database keeps the aggregate. The cache is a local speed-up that any
# clone regenerates by running the scraper.
data/cache/

# --- Local report files ------------------------------------------------------
data/robots_report.json

# --- The database ------------------------------------------------------------
# COMMENTED OUT ON PURPOSE.
#
# data/menu_prices.sqlite is committed, because Streamlit Community Cloud
# deploys straight from this repository and has no other way to reach the
# data. It holds item names and prices only: no page content, no personal
# data, nothing identifying.
#
# Uncomment the next line if the file ever grows past roughly 50 MB, and move
# to a hosted database at that point.
# data/*.sqlite

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# --- Virtual environments ----------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Testing and tooling -----------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Streamlit ---------------------------------------------------------------
# secrets.toml can hold API keys. This project needs none, since the BLS
# endpoint answers without one, and the ignore stays so a future key cannot be
# committed by accident.
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# --- Editors and OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
